// Probe 42 — Cluster I edge case: void-statement `??` (no consumer)
//
// What happens when `vec[i] ?? "x"` is used as a statement with no LHS?
// The value-block result is computed and discarded — but the `_ncc_N`
// scope-exit `OpFreeText` still runs.  Does the stack get left in a
// bad state (next opcode reads garbage from a misaligned slot)?
//
// Two failure modes to look for:
//   (a) Stack-misalignment crash (PANIC at some later opcode).
//   (b) Silent leak of `_ncc_N`'s String (visible via leak gate).
//   (c) Clean — the result is discarded properly.
//
// Pairing: standalone; tests stack-discipline of the void-stmt path.
// Status: cluster I edge-case probe; informs leak-gate exposure.

struct H { items: vector<text> }

fn main() {
  h = H { items: [] };
  h.items += ["present"];
  // Discard the value.  Compiler MAY warn "unused expression" but
  // the bytecode should still run cleanly.
  h.items[0] ?? "fallback";
  // If we get here without a panic, the void-stmt path is clean.
  // Leak gate (separate run with LOFT_STORES=warn) would catch leak.
  println("probe 42 PASSED");
}
